  <p>Be honest about the fourth row. Flat output with a fully implemented platform is the most common situation behind this search, and it does not get better by switching platforms.</p>

  <p><strong>No benchmark sets the crossover point.</strong> There is no published, methodical figure for how many variants a campaign needs, and no independent source defines the volume at which one layer becomes better value than the other. Every number circulating on that question traces back to a company selling variant production. So the table above is built from what each layer does rather than from a threshold, and anyone quoting you a specific asset count as the tipping point is quoting a sales figure.</p>

